1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,570
If one elevator rope snaps, will the car fall?

2
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:08,930
The answer lies in a chain of safety systems, not just one part.

3
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:15,050
The car is suspended by several independent steel ropes, not just one.

4
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:20,810
Each rope is chosen to withstand at least twelve times the load it carries.

5
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:24,207
What if the power goes out?

6
00:00:24,207 --> 00:00:28,470
The machine's spring-applied brake engages on its own and stops the car.

7
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:32,470
And what if the car speeds up out of control?

8
00:00:33,420 --> 00:00:36,913
That's when the overspeed governor stops its separate rope.

9
00:00:36,913 --> 00:00:39,103
This activates the car's safety gear.

10
00:00:39,103 --> 00:00:41,234
Steel wedges grip the guide rails...

11
00:00:41,234 --> 00:00:42,650
and the car stops.

12
00:00:45,020 --> 00:00:47,105
But what if these systems are neglected?

13
00:00:47,105 --> 00:00:49,070
That's when the risk increases.

14
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:55,250
That's why an authorized company services the elevator at least once a month.

15
00:00:56,860 --> 00:01:01,270
And at least once a year, an independent periodic inspection is carried out.

16
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:06,008
The result is shown on a color-coded inspection label.

17
00:01:06,008 --> 00:01:07,074
Red means unsafe.

18
00:01:07,074 --> 00:01:08,930
Don't use that elevator.

19
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:11,874
Check the label before you step in.

20
00:01:11,874 --> 00:01:12,922
What color is yours?

21
00:01:12,922 --> 00:01:14,530
Tell us in the comments.

